WHATNOW

What tam-knox is doing now and what comes next. Read this first;
revise it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-25, with W2

STATE

  Version 0.2.0 on branch dev. Phases P1 (0.1.0-0.1.2) and P2 (0.2.0)
  are complete and pass make test, make sanitize, and idol-check (W1,
  W2).

  Features working in 0.2.0:
  - Multi-repository Source Control sidebar (repository discovery,
    branch name, dirty/clean state, changed files list, ahead/behind
    count, path-scoped staging and committing, and remote sync with
    protected-branch confirmation for main and test).
  - Interactive Branch Checkout and Creation modal (Alt+K or c): lists
    and filters local and remote branches, checks out local or tracking
    remote branches, and creates new branches from HEAD (Alt+N).
  - Stash Management modal (Alt+Z or z): lists stashes, pushes working
    and untracked changes with an optional message (n / s), views stash
    diffs (Enter), applies (a), pops (p), and drops stashes with y/N
    confirmation (d).
  - Side-by-Side Split Diff mode (d, D, Alt+D, or R in Diff Viewer):
    pairs deleted and added lines into aligned Old and New columns with
    dual line-number gutters, synchronized scrolling, and search.
  - Git Graph commit history using the Vertex/Branch/determinePath lane
    layout algorithm from mhutchie.git-graph, with inline ref badges and
    a split Commit Details and Changed Files diff inspector.
  - Folder Explorer tree with live Git status badges.
  - File and Diff Viewer with C11 syntax coloring and tam-view Markdown,
    HTML, and Mermaid rendering, tabs, split panes, command palette, and
    keybinding guidance (g / Ctrl+G).

NEXT

  1. P3 (0.3.0): File tree substring filter, multi-repo batch fetch, and
